# Zod v4 and environment

## Zod v4

- `z.enum()` accepts enum-like objects; `z.nativeEnum()` is deprecated. Use the singular `.enum` accessor.
- `error.flatten()` is deprecated; prefer `z.flattenError(error)`.
- Use top-level formats such as `z.url()` and `z.email()`, not `z.string().url()` or `z.string().email()`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
z.nativeEnum(Status);
z.string().email();
error.flatten();

// ✅ GOOD
z.enum(Status);
z.email();
z.flattenError(error);
```

## Environment

Seven validated vars, all through the `lib/env.ts` singleton — application code never reads `process.env` directly:

- App: `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, `CLERK_SECRET_KEY`, server-only `API_URL` (must not use `NEXT_PUBLIC_`)
- Clerk SDK routing: `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_IN_FALLBACK_REDIRECT_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_SIGN_UP_FALLBACK_REDIRECT_URL`
